-- RULES OF DDL /DML/
-- DDL :
-- 1) CREATE TABLE 
--    RULE 1. THE TABLE NAME /COLUMN_NAME SHOULDN'Y STARTS WITH ANY 
--             NUMBER /SPECIAL CHARACTERS 
--             EX :1EMP / @EMP  ---- IN VALID TABLE_NAME 
--                  EMP1 / EMP@ /E1MP /E@MP ---- VALID TABLE_NAME 
--                  SAME FOR COLUMN_NAME ALSO 
--     RULE 2. THE TABLE_NAME SHOULDN'T REPEATS IN DATABSE 
--     RULE 3. WHILE CREATING TABLE IF WE CREATE PARENT TABLE FIRST AND
--             CHILD TABLE SECOND IT WILL EASY TO CREATE 
     
-- 2) RENAME TABLE 
--     READ THE 1ST RULE OF TABLE_NAME

-- 3) TRUNCATE TABLE 
--    RULE : IF WE ARE TRUNCATING PARENT TABLE ITS NOT POSSIBLE 
--            UNTILL WE REMOVES THE CONNECTION BETWEEN PT AND CT 

-- 4) DROP TABLE 
--     RULE : IF WE WANT TO DROP THE PARENT TABLE WE NEED TO REMEOVE THE CONNECTION THEN WE CAN OTHER TABLE WE CAN DROP EASILY 







-- 5) ALTER : ITS MEANS MODIFICATION OF TABLE 
--      RULE : ALTER COMMAND MOST OF TIME WILL WORKS FOR EMPTY TABLES 
--            EFW COMMANDS IN ALTER WILL WORKS FOR FILLED TABLE 

--     1) ADD COLUMN 
--        RULE : WE CAN ADD COLUMN FOR ANY TABLE IF TABLE IS EMPTY 
--                OR ELSE WE CAN USE NULL CONSTRAINTTO ADD COLUMN 
--               IF WE USE NOT NULL THEN WE CAN ADD COLUMN ONLY EMPTY TABLE 
--      2) DROP COLUMN 
--         THERE IS NO RUELS 
--      3) RENAME COLUMN 
--         COLUMN_NAME RULES WE NEED FOLLOW 
--      4) CHANGE DATATYPE OF COLUMNS 
--         RULE 1 : FOR EMPTY COLUMN WE CAN CHANGE DATATYPES 
--                  IF COLUMN FILLED WITH DATA WE CAN INCREASE THE SIZE OF 
--                  IT BUT WE CANT ABLE CHANGE IT 
--       5) CHANGE NULL TO NOT NULL 
--          RULE1 : FOR PK ITS NOT VALID 
--       6) MAKE PR / FK 
--          RULE FOR PK 1) ONLY ONE PK SHOULD BE PRESENT IN TABLE 
--          RULE FOR FK 1) THE COLUMN SHOULD BE PK IN ANOTHER/ SAME TABLE 
 
--     NOTE FOR ALTER : MOST OF TIME THE ALTER WILL WORK FOR EMPTY                           TABLE   FEW COMMANDS WILL WORK FOR FILLED TABLE












-- DML RULES 
-- 1) INSERT 
--    RULE1 : WE CAN INSERT FOR ANY TABLE BUT WILE INSERTING INTO 
--            CHILD TABLE THE FOREIGN KEY COLUMN VALUE THAT VALUE 
--            SHOULD BE PRESENT IN PARENT TABLE ALSO 

-- 2) DELETE 
--    RULE1 : WE CAN DELETE ANY RECORD FROM THE ANY TABLE BUT 
--            WHILE DELETING RECORDS FROM THE PARENT TABLE WE NEED TO 
--            REMOVE THE CONNECTION ELSE ITS NOT POSSIBLE 

-- 3) UPDATE 
--    RULE1 : WE CAN UPDATE ANY TABLE BUT WHILE UPDATING 
--            THE VALUE OF PARENT TABLE IN THAT THE PK WE
--            NEED TO USE THE VALUES WHICH ARE PRESENT IN CHILD TABLE /NULL  
--            WHERE AS UPDATING THE CHILD TABLE FK VALUE WE NEED 
--            USE THE VALUE WHICH ARE PRESENT IN PARENT TABLE 



















